    [Doc][Misc] Add boundary/edge-case checklist to PR template (#18751)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Recently a code-merge incident occurred because boundary values were not
    checked before merging. To prevent recurrence, this PR adds a **Testing
    checklist** to the PR template so contributors self-check
    boundary/edge-case scenarios before requesting review.
    
    Changes:
    - **`.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`**: Add a `### Checklist` section
    with a `Testing` group covering:
    - Boundary / edge-case coverage (empty input, single/zero element,
    min/max values, off-by-one, sequence-length limits, integer overflow)
      - Regression test for bug fixes
      - Error / failure path coverage
      - Meaningful & reliable tests
      - Performance impact
    - **`AGENTS.md`**: Sync `Test Coverage Guidelines` and `Review Checklist
    · Testing` to require boundary/edge-case scenario coverage, keeping the
    guide consistent with the PR template.
    
    The checklist items are distilled from mainstream open-source
    communities (vLLM upstream, PyTorch, Kubernetes, HuggingFace
    Transformers, TensorFlow, OpenAI Triton, RAPIDS cuDF), adapted to this
    project's conventions.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No code behavior change. Only the PR template and contributor guide are
    updated. Contributors will see a new checklist section when opening PRs.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `markdownlint` passes on `AGENTS.md` (config: `.markdownlint.yaml`).
    `PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` is excluded from markdownlint per
    `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.
    - Manually verified the rendered PR template displays the checklist
    correctly.
    - No unit tests needed (documentation/template-only change).
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: hejianping <hejianping7@huawei.com>

